The following is a multiple choice question about college computer science.

Any set of Boolean operators that is sufficient to represent all Boolean expressions is said to be complete. Which of the following is NOT complete?

A. {AND, NOT}
B. {NOT, OR}
C. {AND, OR}
D. {NAND}

Answer with only the letter (A, B, C, or D) of the correct option.

The following is a multiple choice question about college mathematics.

Let R be a ring and let U and V be (two-sided) ideals of R. Which of the following must also be ideals of R ?
I. {u + v : u \in and v \in V}
II. {uv : u \in U and v \in V}
III. {x : x \in U and x \in V}

A. II only
B. III only
C. I and II only
D. I and III only

Answer with only the letter (A, B, C, or D) of the correct option.

The following is a multiple choice question about formal logic.

S Select the best translation into predicate logic. Some kind people help some endangered species. (Ex: x is endangered; Kx: x is kind; Px: x is a person; Sx: x is a species; Hxy: x helps y)

A. (∃x){(Kx • Px) • (∃y)[(Ey • Sy) • Hxy]}
B. (∃x)(∃y){[(Kx • Sx) • (Ey • Py)] • Hxy}
C. (∃x)(∃y){[(Kx • Sx) • (Ey • Py)] • Hyx}
D. (∃x)(∃y){[(Kx • Px) • (Ey • Sy)] ⊃ Hxy}

Answer with only the letter (A, B, C, or D) of the correct option.

The following is a multiple choice question about high school computer science.

Which of the following is the hexadecimal representation of the decimal number 231_{10} ?

A. 17_{16}
B. E4_{16}
C. E7_{16}
D. F4_{16}

Answer with only the letter (A, B, C, or D) of the correct option.

The following is a multiple choice question about high school computer science.

Let l = [1,2,2,3,4]. In Python3, what is a possible output of set(l)?

A. {1}
B. {1,2,2,3,4}
C. {1,2,3,4}
D. {4,3,2,2,1}

Answer with only the letter (A, B, C, or D) of the correct option.

The following is a multiple choice question about high school mathematics.

Three points are chosen randomly and independently on a circle. What is the probability that all three pairwise distances between the points are less than the radius of the circle?

A. \frac{1}{20}
B. \frac{1}{32}
C. \frac{1}{12}
D. \frac{1}{16}

Answer with only the letter (A, B, C, or D) of the correct option.
